[{"commit":{"message":"Support more than one group specified in jdk.tls.namedGroups in TLS system tests"},"files":[{"filename":"src\/jipherTest\/java\/com\/oracle\/jiphertest\/helpers\/TlsServer.java"},{"filename":"src\/systemTest\/java\/com\/oracle\/systest\/tls\/TlsSystemTest.java"}],"sha":"6876e5393c2c63ef342975765b23a808f83cd80c"},{"commit":{"message":"Support for Quantum-Resistant Module-Lattice-Based Algorithms\n\nImplemented support for:\n* ML-KEM key encapsulation mechanism (KEM) as defined in NIST FIPS 203.\n* ML-DSA digital signature scheme as defined in NIST FIPS 204.\n\nSupport for the following services has been added:\n* KEM:  ML-KEM, ML-KEM-512, ML-KEM-768, ML-KEM-1024\n* KeyFactory: ML-KEM,  ML-KEM-512, ML-KEM-768, ML-KEM-1024, ML-DSA, ML-DSA-44, ML-DSA-65, ML-DSA-87\n* KeyPairGenerator: ML-KEM, ML-KEM-512, ML-KEM-768, ML-KEM-1024, ML-DSA, ML-DSA-44, ML-DSA-65, ML-DSA-87\n* Signature: ML-DSA, ML-DSA-44, ML-DSA-65, ML-DSA-87\n\nAll three PKCS #8 privateKey CHOICE options (\"seed\", \"expandedKey\", and \"both\") are supported at both encoding and decoding for ML-KEM and ML-DSA private keys.\n\nTLS testing using the SunJSSE to provide the protocol stack and JipherJCE providing cryptography has been extended to test TLS 1.3 hybrid key exchange name groups:\n * X25519MLKEM768\n * SecP256r1MLKEM768\n * SecP384r1MLKEM1024"},"files":[{"filename":"gradle.properties"},{"filename":"jacoco.gradle"},{"filename":"src\/intTest\/java\/com\/oracle\/test\/integration\/kem\/KemInitTest.java"},{"filename":"src\/intTest\/java\/com\/oracle\/test\/integration\/kem\/KemMethodTest.java"},{"filename":"src\/intTest\/java\/com\/oracle\/test\/integration\/kem\/KemVectorTest.java"},{"filename":"src\/intTest\/java\/com\/oracle\/test\/integration\/keyfactory\/MlDsaKeyFactoryNegTest.java"},{"filename":"src\/intTest\/java\/com\/oracle\/test\/integration\/keyfactory\/MlDsaKeyFactoryVectorTest.java"},{"filename":"src\/intTest\/java\/com\/oracle\/test\/integration\/keyfactory\/MlKemKey